{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "fc", "rep": 200, "hyps": [{"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Raising an already large Adam step size causes divergence and collapse to majority-class accuracy, as in probes 13-16."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At tiny learning rates the network is undertrained after 243 epochs, so a larger step gives large gains (probes 9-12)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "batch_size", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Large batches mean fewer updates per epoch, so increasing the step size compensates more strongly (probes 5, 11)."}, {"edit_param": "batch_size", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "lower", "why": "With a small learning rate, fewer updates from a larger batch leave the model further undertrained (probes 21-23, 33)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At low learning rates, extra layers add capacity and faster effective fitting without instability (probes 61, 62, 65, 66, 69, 70)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deeper ReLU nets are more prone to instability and dead units at high step sizes (probes 64, 72, 78)."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "When L2 is already strong, increasing it further over-regularizes toward underfitting on every dataset (probes 89-92), while it is negligible at small alpha."}, {"edit_param": "width", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "width", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding u